Commits consulted while implementing note2web's driver
--------------------------------------------------------

- Spike commit (T-08, GitHub issue #13, 2026-07-25):
  `4754a2b62686570cca46690d101079e80cf6ae66`
- Current `master` as of 2026-08-17 (issue #72 implementation date):
  `4754a2b62686570cca46690d101079e80cf6ae66`

Both are the same commit — `git ls-remote
https://github.com/threeplanetssoftware/apple_cloud_notes_parser.git master`
returned this SHA on 2026-08-17, confirming upstream had not moved since the
T-08 spike. `ruby/note2web_export.rb` requires (directly or transitively) the
following files from that commit: `lib/KeyedArchive.rb`,
`lib/AppleDecrypter.rb`, `lib/AppleBackup.rb`, `lib/AppleBackupMac.rb`,
`lib/AppleNote.rb`, `lib/AppleNoteStore.rb`, `lib/AppleNotesFolder.rb`,
`lib/AppleNotesAccount.rb`, `lib/AppleCloudKitRecord.rb`, and the
`AppleNotesEmbeddedObject` subclasses they transitively require.

How note2web uses it (usage form)
----------------------------------

1. The user clones `apple_cloud_notes_parser` to a local directory (external
   to note2web) and runs `bundle install` there, per that project's own
   README (see this repository's README.md "Setup" section).
2. note2web's own `ruby/note2web_export.rb` is executed with
   `--parser-lib <clone>/lib` and, at runtime, `require`s specific files
   from that directory. `cwd` is set to the clone's root so that
   `bundle exec` can find its `Gemfile`.
3. note2web's script does not modify, copy, or redistribute any file from
   the clone. It only calls documented instance methods on the classes it
   loads (e.g. `AppleNote#generate_html`, `AppleNote#prepare_json`,
   `AppleNotesFolder#name`) to read already-decoded note/folder data, and
   writes its own output files under a note2web-controlled output directory.

